From: brkosebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: Quiet polled cover inputs and exclusive RTC event

Collapse the intermediate IRQ-driven cover change and its storm fix into the final polled-cover implementation, keeping PMU events 48/58 masked. Reserve event 16 exclusively for the RTC while retaining Tristar event-72 wake and parent-line protection. Add the one-shot RTC alarm interface and accept both directions of the known Apple current-grant request; do not fabricate a host grant or claim Mac charging is fixed. Cover wake remains deferred.

Integration fixups are folded into the final delta. Device observations apply
to the integration build; the isolated topic requires qualification.

Assisted-by: LLM
---

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/composite.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/composite.c
index 1da3effb2..14e87fbc8 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/composite.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/composite.c
@@ -968,7 +968,7 @@ static int composite_apple_current_limit(struct usb_composite_dev *cdev,
 					 u16 w_value, u16 w_index)
 {
 	cdev->apple_extra_ma = (s16)w_index;
-	DBG(cdev, "Apple host current grant: extra %d mA, suspend %d mA\n",
+	dev_info(&cdev->gadget->dev, "Apple host current grant: extra %d mA, suspend %d mA\n",
 	    (s16)w_index, (s16)w_value);
 	composite_vbus_draw(cdev, cdev->vbus_draw_ma);
 	return 0;
@@ -2221,7 +2221,7 @@ composite_setup(struct usb_gadget *gadget, const struct usb_ctrlrequest *ctrl)
 			goto check_value;
 		}
 
-		if (ctrl->bRequestType == (USB_DIR_OUT | USB_TYPE_VENDOR |
+		if ((ctrl->bRequestType & ~USB_DIR_IN) == (USB_TYPE_VENDOR |
 					   USB_RECIP_DEVICE) &&
 		    ctrl->bRequest == USB_APPLE_REQ_CURRENT_LIMIT && !w_length &&
 		    le16_to_cpu(cdev->desc.idVendor) == USB_APPLE_VENDOR_ID) {
